---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageCTA from '../components/PageCTA.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How to Convert TXT to Image — 3-Step Guide | txttoimage"
  description="Learn how to convert text files to PNG, JPG, or WebP in 3 easy steps. Complete guide with customization, format recommendations, and troubleshooting. No software needed."
  path="/how-it-works"
>
  <section class="min-h-[50dvh] flex flex-col pt-28 pb-12">
    <div class="flex-1 flex flex-col max-w-3xl mx-auto w-full px-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-emerald-600 font-medium mb-3"><a href="/" class="hover:underline">txttoimage</a> &rsaquo; How It Works</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 leading-[1.15]">How to Convert TXT to Image — The Complete Guide</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">Everything you need to know about converting text files into images. Detailed step-by-step instructions, customization guides, format recommendations, troubleshooting, and pro tips. No software to install, no accounts, no uploads.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="py-4 bg-white border-b border-zinc-200 sticky top-14 z-40">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 flex items-center gap-1.5 overflow-x-auto">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-400 uppercase tracking-wider mr-2 shrink-0">On this page:</span>
      <a href="#steps" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">3 Steps</a>
      <a href="#settings" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">Settings</a>
      <a href="#formats" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">Formats</a>
      <a href="#tips" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">Pro Tips</a>
      <a href="#troubleshooting" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">Troubleshooting</a>
      <a href="#faq" class="shrink-0 text-xs text-zinc-500 hover:text-emerald-600 bg-zinc-50 hover:bg-emerald-50 border border-zinc-200 hover:border-emerald-200 rounded-full px-3 py-1.5 transition-colors">FAQ</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section id="steps" class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">3 Steps to Convert Text to Image</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">The entire process takes under 5 seconds. All processing happens in your browser — your files never leave your device.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-10">
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4"><span class="w-10 h-10 bg-emerald-500 text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg shrink-0">1</span><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 text-lg">Upload Your Text File</h3></div>
          <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">Drag and drop your file onto the upload zone or click to browse your computer. The converter accepts any text-based file: .txt, .md, .csv, .log, .json, .xml, .yml, .yaml, .cfg, .ini, .conf, .env, .toml, .html, .css, and source code from 13+ programming languages.</p>
          <div class="bg-zinc-50 border border-zinc-100 rounded-lg p-4"><p class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-400 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">What happens</p><p class="text-xs text-zinc-500">The file is read using the browser's FileReader API. Content is loaded into local memory only — no data is transmitted over the network. You will see the file name, size in KB, line count, and a scrollable preview of the first 2,000 characters. A green notification confirms successful loading. The file size limit is 10MB — a browser memory safeguard, not a service restriction.</p></div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4"><span class="w-10 h-10 bg-emerald-500 text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg shrink-0">2</span><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 text-lg">Customize the Output</h3></div>
          <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">The settings panel gives you full control over the output image. All settings update when you re-convert — you can experiment until the result looks right.</p>

          <div class="space-y-3 mt-3">
            <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded shrink-0 mt-0.5">Format</span><div><p class="text-sm text-zinc-700 font-medium">PNG (lossless), JPG (smaller), or WebP (best compression)</p><p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 mt-0.5">PNG for documentation and code — perfect quality. JPG for email and messaging — 50-80% smaller files. WebP for websites — smallest file size with good quality. See our <a href="/txt-to-png" class="text-emerald-600 hover:underline">format comparison</a> for detailed guidance.</p></div></div>
            <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded shrink-0 mt-0.5">Font</span><div><p class="text-sm text-zinc-700 font-medium">Monospace, Sans Serif, or Serif at 10-32px</p><p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 mt-0.5">Monospace for code, logs, and data — preserves column alignment. Sans Serif for modern clean documents. Serif for formal or literary content.</p></div></div>
            <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded shrink-0 mt-0.5">Colors</span><div><p class="text-sm text-zinc-700 font-medium">Custom background and text colors</p><p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 mt-0.5">Popular: white background with near-black text for documents; dark background (#1e1e1e) with light text (#e0e0e0) for terminal-style output.</p></div></div>
            <div class="flex gap-4"><span class="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 px-2 py-0.5 rounded shrink-0 mt-0.5">Layout</span><div><p class="text-sm text-zinc-700 font-medium">Padding (20-80px) and aspect ratio (16:9, 4:3, 1:1, 9:16, and more)</p><p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 mt-0.5">16:9 = widescreen (1280x720px) for social media. 4:3 = slides. 1:1 = Instagram. 9:16 = mobile. Use 40-60px padding for a polished look.</p></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-4"><span class="w-10 h-10 bg-emerald-500 text-white rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg shrink-0">3</span><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900 text-lg">Convert and Download</h3></div>
          <p class="text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">Click Convert to Image. The text renders on an HTML5 Canvas with word wrapping applied to fit your chosen aspect ratio. The result appears instantly in the preview panel. Click Download Image to save the file to your device — the file keeps your original name with the new extension (.png, .jpg, or .webp).</p>
          <div class="bg-zinc-50 border border-zinc-100 rounded-lg p-4"><p class="text-xs font-semibold text-zinc-400 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Pro tip</p><p class="text-xs text-zinc-500">You can change settings and hit Convert again without re-uploading. The file stays in memory until you click Remove. There is no limit on conversion attempts — experiment freely.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="settings" class="py-16 bg-zinc-100">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">Understanding the Output Settings</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Every setting in the converter exists for a reason. Here is what each one does and when to use it.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6"><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900">Output Format</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">PNG: lossless, sharp, 200-600KB per image. Best for code, documentation, archiving. JPG: lossy, compact, 80-200KB per image. Best for email, messaging, social media. WebP: modern, smallest size, 60-250KB per image. Best for websites. Note: some older email clients do not display WebP images.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6"><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900">Font Family</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Monospace: equal-width characters — critical for code, logs, CSV, and any content where alignment matters. Sans Serif: clean, modern, variable-width — good for general documents. Serif: traditional, formal — suitable for long-form literary content and academic papers.</p></div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-6"><h3 class="font-semibold text-zinc-900">Aspect Ratio</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">16:9 (1280x720): standard widescreen. 4:3 (960x720): traditional slides. 1:1 (800x800): social media squares. 3:2 (900x600): photo ratio. 9:16 (450x800): mobile portrait. 3:4 (600x800): portrait documents. The converter renders at the exact pixel dimensions listed — no upscaling or downscaling.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="formats" class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">Supported Input File Formats</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">The converter reads any file as raw text. Here is the complete categorized list of supported file types. Any file that can be opened in a text editor can be converted.</p>

      <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Plain Text & Documents</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5"><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.txt</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.text</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.log</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.md</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.markdown</code></div></div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Structured Data</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5"><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.csv</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.json</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.xml</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.yml</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.yaml</code></div></div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Configuration</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5"><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.cfg</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.ini</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.conf</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.env</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.toml</code></div></div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Web & Markup</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5"><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.html</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.css</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.svg</code></div></div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Programming Languages</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5"><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.js</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.ts</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.py</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.java</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.c</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.cpp</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.h</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.rb</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.go</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.rs</code></div></div>
        <div class="bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-900 mb-3">Scripts & SQL</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5"><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.sh</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.bat</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.ps1</code><code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 text-zinc-600 px-2 py-1 rounded-md">.sql</code></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="tips" class="py-16 bg-zinc-100">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">Pro Tips for Best Results</h2>
      <ul class="mt-8 space-y-4">
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold shrink-0">&check;</span><div><strong class="text-zinc-800">For code: Monospace + dark background + 14px to 16px.</strong> This combination looks professional and is immediately recognizable to developers.</div></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold shrink-0">&check;</span><div><strong class="text-zinc-800">For documents: Sans Serif + white background + 16px.</strong> Clean and readable, suitable for general-purpose document sharing.</div></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold shrink-0">&check;</span><div><strong class="text-zinc-800">For social media code posts: 16:9 + PNG.</strong> PNG at 16:9 with a dark background gets the most engagement for developer content on Twitter/X.</div></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold shrink-0">&check;</span><div><strong class="text-zinc-800">For email attachments: JPG + 16:9.</strong> JPG reduces file size by 50-80% compared to PNG, keeping email attachments well under provider limits.</div></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold shrink-0">&check;</span><div><strong class="text-zinc-800">For large files: filter before converting.</strong> Extract the relevant section of a large file before conversion. A focused excerpt is more useful than a 5,000-line dump.</div></li>
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl p-5"><span class="text-emerald-500 font-bold shrink-0">&check;</span><div><strong class="text-zinc-800">For presentations: 4:3 or 16:9 + 40px padding.</strong> Use the aspect ratio matching your slide deck and generous padding for a polished look.</div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="troubleshooting" class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">Troubleshooting</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Solutions to the most common issues users encounter.</p>

      <dl class="mt-8 space-y-1">
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">My file loads but the preview shows garbled text. <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">This usually means the file uses an encoding the browser cannot read as text. The converter uses UTF-8 encoding by default. If your file is in a different encoding (like UTF-16 or ISO-8859-1), try opening it in a text editor and re-saving it as UTF-8 before converting.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">The output image cuts off my text. <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">The converter renders up to 5,000 lines and shows a truncation notice if your content exceeds this. Solutions: (1) Reduce the font size to fit more lines per image. (2) Switch to a taller aspect ratio like 3:4 or 9:16. (3) Extract the relevant section of your file before conversion.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">The converter does not recognize my file type. <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">The converter checks file extensions and MIME types to confirm the file is text-based. If your file has an unusual extension, try renaming it to .txt before uploading. The content will still be read correctly as plain text. You can also try copying and pasting the content into a new .txt file.</div>
        </details>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" class="py-16 bg-zinc-100">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-zinc-900 tracking-tight">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <dl class="mt-8 space-y-1">
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">How long does conversion take? <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Under 1 second for typical files (under 1MB, under 1,000 lines). Larger files near the 10MB or 5,000-line limits may take 1-2 seconds. There is no server upload or download time — the only delay is the local canvas rendering, which is nearly instantaneous on modern hardware.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">Can I use this offline? <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">Yes, partially. Once the page is loaded in your browser, all processing is client-side and does not require an internet connection. The fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, so if you are offline when the page first loads, Sans Serif and Serif may fall back to system fonts. Monospace will still work correctly using the browser's built-in monospace font. For fully offline use, you can save the page as a complete HTML file.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="group bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-xl">
          <summary class="px-5 py-4 cursor-pointer font-medium text-zinc-900 text-sm flex items-center justify-between">Is there a way to batch convert multiple files? <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform ml-2 shrink-0" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm text-zinc-500 leading-relaxed">The current version processes one file at a time. However, since each conversion takes only a few seconds and there is no daily limit, you can convert files sequentially very quickly. For bulk conversion needs, simply repeat the process for each file — there is no throttling or restriction on the number of conversions.</div>
        </details>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wide">Related Pages</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/txt-to-png" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">TXT to PNG</a>
        <a href="/txt-to-jpg" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">TXT to JPG</a>
        <a href="/code-to-image" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">Code to Image</a>
        <a href="/compare" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">Compare Tools</a>
        <a href="/" class="text-sm text-zinc-600 bg-white border border-zinc-200 rounded-full px-4 py-2 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-600 transition-colors">Home</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PageCTA title="Ready to Try It Yourself?" description="Drop a text file and see the converter in action. It takes less than 5 seconds from upload to download." buttonText="Start Converting" />

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
